  "gang": "dragonforce",
  "displayName": "DragonForce",
  "aliases": [
    "DragonForce Ransomware Cartel"
  ],
  "status": "active",
  "activeSince": "2023",
  "lineage": "Encryptors built from leaked LockBit 3.0 and Conti v3 code; operates a white-label 'cartel' model and has been used by Scattered Spider-linked affiliates",
  "summary": "DragonForce launched in 2023 with a LockBit 3.0-based locker and later a Conti v3-derived build, rebranding in 2025 as a 'cartel' that lets affiliates white-label its ransomware. Intrusions range from valid-credential access to web servers with Cobalt Strike, SystemBC, Mimikatz and AdFind, to 2025 Scattered Spider-style help-desk social engineering against UK retailers and an MSP compromise via chained SimpleHelp RMM vulnerabilities used to push ransomware to downstream customers. The Conti-based locker supports BYOVD EDR killing (truesight.sys, rentdrv2.sys), ESXi/Linux targeting and clears event logs after encryption.",
  "uniqueTraits": [
    "Supply-chain style MSP attack: SimpleHelp CVE-2024-57727/57726/57728 chain, then the MSP's RMM pushes ransomware to customers",
    "Scattered Spider-affiliated help-desk social engineering (vishing, MFA fatigue, SIM swap) in 2025 retail attacks",
    "BYOVD via truesight.sys and rentdrv2.sys built into the locker (use_sys option)",
    "White-label cartel model with LockBit 3.0 and Conti v3 derived lockers"
  ],
  "insufficientReporting": false,
